# Findings of the credential scan that were read and are not credentials. The 'Credential scan'
# workflow runs betterleaks with Tools/Invoke-CredentialScan.ps1, which passes this file to it.
# A line is one finding: the commit that added the text, the file, the rule, and the line number.
#
# Every entry is a line of a commit that was made before the scan existed, and none of the text
# is in the files today. A commit does not change, so an entry stays valid.
#
# Add a line only for a value that was read and is not a credential, and prefer changing the
# value so that the scan does not report it. A real credential is revoked first: a commit that
# removes it leaves it in the history, where the scan and everyone else still find it.

